{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/964105-combat-example-and-other-beginner-questions","id":964105,"title":"Combat example and other beginner questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-05T23:25:56-07:00","id":964105,"title":"Combat example and other beginner questions","content":"As I am fairly new to CoD and plan to start my first session, I wanted to ask if there is an elaborated example for combat? The rulebook lacks a couple of example to several topics.<br /> <br /> In addition (don't want to appear greedy) is there a cheat sheet for CoD? There are plenty for the older editions but I didn't find one for the actual one.<br /> <br /> Also I'd like to focus on &quot;human&quot; non-monster PCs with a lot of freedom in the setting. My plan is to use the MMO The Secret World as a setting for my group. Which material would you advise? Maybe a tad Mage as the heroes might utilize some magic? Can chars created with the CoD core books &quot;awake&quot; at a later time?<br /> It revolves around secret societies like the Templar or the illuminati. Would those &quot;conspiracies&quot; mentioned in Hunter the Vigil qualify for those secret societies?<br /> <br /> I would also like to include a heavy lovecraftian touch into my game. Are there sources/material helping to generate such creatures like deep ones, shoggoths and the like? Are they included in one of the setting books?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T23:49:03-07:00","id":964114,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have much experience with actual play of the game so I can't be of much help with a combat example/cheat sheet. But when it comes to running a game like that, the Chronicles of Darkness book covers most of what you would need, though Second Sight can also be useful.<br /> <br /> Using just the core book can represent the magic players use through eventually giving them supernatural merits or allow them to &quot;craft&quot; magical effects using the crafting rules to make wards, trickets and such. Second Sight is a book focused around mortals with a bit of magical power through different types of traditions, though many mechanical aspects of the book have been put into the Chronicles of Darkness book in the form of the previously mentioned Supernatural merits. <br /> <br /> For conspiracies you can mechanically represent them as mystery cults, and you gain benefits in them as you take the mystery cult initiation merit (and you can say that players cannot take supernatural merits until they gain a supernatural merit from their mystery cult). Though some of he conspiracies mentioned in Hunter could work as secret societies that you desire, though they have more specific flavour and aren't &quot;rule the world from the shadows&quot; like the illuminati/templars.<br /> <br /> For putting in lovecraftian abominations, Chronicles of Darkness has rules for making your own monsters referred to as &quot;Horrors&quot;, which should allow you to create Deep Ones, Shoggoths, Ghouls, Mi-Go, etc. without much trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:12:29-07:00","id":964209,"title":"","content":"Thanks milo, Second Sight is exactly what I was looking for. Is there any need for converting anything from Second Sight to fit in CoD or can I just use the content as written?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:28:51-07:00","id":964213,"title":"","content":"The Secret World is probably best emulated by the game Hunter: the Vigil, I would suggest. I highly recommend getting that book. Or waiting for the 2nd edition to come out, which I think is currently in the works. There are also magical endowments that you can use in place of rituals as necessary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T04:59:34-07:00","id":964221,"title":"","content":"Hunter: the Vigil is indeed something I actually anticipate very much and I'll wait until 2nd comes out.<br /> <br /> I was told mortals in H:tV are very squishy, so to say fingerfood for all those monsters. Btw, is Mage the Awakening also suited for mortals or are mages too powerful in comparison to normal human PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:11:43-07:00","id":964226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Thanks milo, Second Sight is exactly what I was looking for. Is there any need for converting anything from Second Sight to fit in CoD or can I just use the content as written?</span> </div> </div> </div>I think it should probably work as written, might need a tiny tweak here and there. But from a skim it seems fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Btw, is Mage the Awakening also suited for mortals or are mages too powerful in comparison to normal human PCs?</span> </div> </div> </div> Mages are often argued to be one of the most powerful playable characters in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-06-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:31:09-07:00","id":964237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/964105-combat-example-and-other-beginner-questions?p=964221#post964221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was told mortals in H:tV are very squishy, so to say fingerfood for all those monsters. Btw, is Mage the Awakening also suited for mortals or are mages too powerful in comparison to normal human PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div> Generally, mortals are weak against monsters, simply because they lack the innate magical abilities others do. That said, hunters also lack specific weaknesses like supernaturals do.<br /> <br /> And, yes, Mage is unsuitable for mortals PC game. Vastly so. Not just in terms of power, but in terms of changes to plot and theme, as well as raw incompatability due to Dissonance. That said, you might be able to get away with some Proximi (mini-mages equivalent to a ghoul in power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T05:36:25-07:00","id":964241,"title":"","content":"I'm very content with the low magic as depicted in Second Sight. I guess if some o f the players want to dabble with &quot;high&quot; magic all should, otherwise they won't be balanced.<br /> <br /> Funny, I'm indifferent to PCs playing powerful monsters, the playing mortals part though sounds most fun to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:58:35-07:00","id":964322,"title":"","content":"As a <b>Secret World</b> fan myself, I can say that Templars works as London Adamantine Arrows, Illuminati as New York Mysterium ( with a bit Guardians of Veil ) and Dragons as Silver Ladder ( I guess? ) from <b>Mage</b>. Still, game is evenly in middle between <b>Hunter</b> and <b>Mage </b>power level, but if you want to emulate more 'low power' feel, I would go with <b>Hunter</b>. Not going with Mage Orders, I would work on Conspiracies as Mystery Cult Initiation groups, with special powers on their own - canon <b>Hunter</b> groups like <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> or <i>Cherion Group</i> each have their own 'magic' with variety of effects, enough for 'secret society monster hunters' idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/964105-combat-example-and-other-beginner-questions?p=964221#post964221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter: the Vigil is indeed something I actually anticipate very much and I'll wait until 2nd comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you will wait a large time for it - <b>Hunter: the Vigil </b>2E has <i>maybe</i> ended recruitment for writers, we do not have any news on coming Open Development issues in blog posts from last December. To me, we will not see this book till late 2018. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If we see it earlier, I can eat my hat!<br /> <br /> I would advise you to get <b>Hunter: The Vigil </b>1E, <b>Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook </b>and <b>Mortal Remains</b> Appendix ( it's <b>Hunter</b>'s 'patch' to 2E rules ) - you can easily run on this collection <b>Hunter</b> game. I was playing in short chronicle of this myself, a year ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belisarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/964105-combat-example-and-other-beginner-questions?p=964221#post964221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, is Mage the Awakening also suited for mortals or are mages too powerful in comparison to normal human PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are leauge of their own. But, yeah, you could have 'traditional wizards' from Proximi that would much better work with <b>Hunter</b> level of plot. <b>Mage</b> is great fun to run, but I would not do any crossover with it lower than Major Template - I even plan now to add <b>Promethean</b> to one of mine <b>Mage</b> groups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-06-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:42:49-07:00","id":964342,"title":"","content":"Thinking more on subject, you could even take out<b> Hunter: The Vigil</b> 1E and <b>Mortal Remains</b> from equation if you really only want to recreate <b>Secret World</b> organisations. All mechanical burden has went to <b>Chronicles of Darkness Ruleboo</b>k, <b>H:tV</b> and <b>Mortal Remains</b> are only for very Hunter specific things, like Conspiracy write-ups and their Endowments.<br /> <br /> But <b>Hunter</b> has very cool and interesting organisation, so I would still point to read at least corebook of gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:00:21-07:00","id":964400,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the inspiration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So far I'm going with CoD core rulebook, Second Sight, Hunter: the Vigil and Hunter: Mortal Remains. Those four should equip me for my endeavor to run a game by myself. <br /> Btw, is there a community for hangout sessions? Practicing a bit before launching a chronicle myself might be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}